}

NOTES: Build plates as PlaneGeometry rotated into horizontal planes with a MeshBasicMaterial gradient texture; instance the red arrows with InstancedMesh (cylinder shaft + cone head) for the ~150 plate arrows. Cube edges via LineSegments on EdgesGeometry; each of the six faces is a separate clickable Mesh with raycasting, rendered double-sided and transparent, with an outward normal arrow and a floating label 'Φ = E·n̂A = …' that appears on selection. Render order / depthWrite:false on transparent faces and the diagonal plane to avoid sorting artifacts against the interior arrows. Vertex letters and plate charge labels as CSS2D/sprite overlays so they stay screen-facing under orbit. For the 'Net flux' toggle, animate the +EA and −EA bar/arrow contributions sliding together and annihilating into a single 'Φ_net = 0' readout.

